---

<div class="home">
  <section class="hero" id="about">
    <div>
      <h1>Mathematician turned <i>AI safety</i> researcher.</h1>
      <p>
        I'm Samantha, a machine learning researcher in New York. I want to understand how AI systems
        work inside, mechanistically and behaviorally, as a foundation for aligning, monitoring and
        controlling them.
      </p>
      <p>
        Before this I did a Ph.D. in pure math at Rutgers–Newark, where I proved the local
        Gan–Gross–Prasad conjecture for tempered representations of general spin groups, part of the
        Langlands program.
      </p>
      <div class="contact">
        {contactLinks.map((link) => (
          <a href={link.href} target={link.external ? "_blank" : undefined} rel={link.external ? "noreferrer" : undefined}>{link.label}</a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="portrait">
      <img src="/home/portrait.jpg" alt="Samantha Pease" width="350" height="440" />
      <RootMark class="portrait-mark" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="timeline" id="research">
    <div class="side-label"><h2>Now</h2><p>AI safety research</p></div>
    <div class="entries">
      <div class="entry">
        <div class="year">2026</div>
        <div>
          <h3><a href="/project-writeups/olmo3-neuron-explorer/">Olmo 3 Neuron Explorer</a></h3>
          <p>Single neurons in Olmo 3: their training documents and steered replies, with shared strings highlighted.</p>
        </div>
        <a class="thumb-link" href="/project-writeups/olmo3-neuron-explorer/"><img class="thumb" src="/home/thumb-neurons.png" alt="Steering-strength curves for six Olmo 3 neurons" loading="lazy" /></a>
      </div>
      <div class="entry">
        <div class="year">2026</div>
        <div>
          <h3><a href="/project-writeups/retraining-unlearning/">Free Recovery: Does LLM Unlearning Actually Remove Knowledge?</a></h3>
          <p>Retrain an "unlearned" model on part of what it forgot and the rest starts coming back. Across eight methods, the knowledge is suppressed, not erased.</p>
        </div>
        <a class="thumb-link" href="/project-writeups/retraining-unlearning/"><img class="thumb" src="/home/thumb-unlearning.png" alt="Chart of knowledge recovered after retraining unlearned models" loading="lazy" /></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="timeline s-math" id="math">
    <div class="side-label"><h2>Before</h2><p>Mathematics</p></div>
    <div class="entries">
      <div class="entry">
        <div class="year">2026</div>
        <div>
          <h3><a href="https://doi.org/doi:10.7282/t3-qb3s-s249" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">The Local Gan–Gross–Prasad Conjecture for General Spin Groups</a></h3>
          <p>
            My dissertation, advised by <a href="https://sites.rutgers.edu/chen-wan/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Chen Wan</a>, proves the conjecture for
            tempered representations via a local trace formula, extending work of Waldspurger for
            special orthogonal groups and Beuzart-Plessis for unitary groups.
          </p>
          <p class="more">
            I'm now <a href="https://github.com/SamPease/GSpinGGP" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">formalizing it in Lean</a>, with the proof written by AI agents under my
            direction. The <a href={BLUEPRINT}>blueprint</a>'s dependency graph, pictured, shows every step and its status.
          </p>
        </div>
        <a class="thumb-link dep-graph" id="gspinggp-graph" href={DEP_GRAPH} aria-label="Open the live dependency graph of the Lean formalization">
          <img class="thumb fill" src="/home/thumb-depgraph.png" alt="Dependency graph of the Lean formalization" loading="lazy" />
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class="entry no-thumb">
        <div class="year">2020</div>
        <div>
          <h3><a href="/pruv.pdf" target="_blank">Computing Values of Symmetric Square L-Functions using Ichino's Pullback Formula</a></h3>
          <p>Undergraduate honors thesis at Duke, computed in Sage. <a href="/Computing%20Values%20of%20Symmetric%20Square%20L-Functions%20using%20Ichino%E2%80%99s.pptx" target="_blank">Slides</a>.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="entry no-thumb">
        <div class="year">2018</div>
        <div><h3><a href="/MATH_502.pdf" target="_blank">Constructible Numbers and Regular n-gons</a></h3></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="timeline s-built" id="projects">
    <div class="side-label"><h2>Built</h2><p>Side projects</p></div>
    <div class="entries">
      {built.map((item) => (
        <div class={item.thumb ? "entry" : "entry no-thumb"}>
          <div class="year">{item.year}</div>
          <div>
            <h3><a href={item.href} target={item.href.startsWith("/project-writeups/") ? undefined : "_blank"}>{item.title}</a></h3>
            <p>{item.text}</p>
          </div>
          {item.thumb && (
            <a class="thumb-link" href={item.href} target={item.href.startsWith("/project-writeups/") ? undefined : "_blank"} tabindex="-1">
              <img class="thumb fill" src={item.thumb} alt={item.alt} loading="lazy" />
            </a>
          )}
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="timeline s-taught" id="teaching">
    <div class="side-label"><h2>Taught</h2><p>2017–2026</p></div>
    <div class="entries">
      <div class="entry no-thumb"><div class="year">Rutgers</div><div><p>Taught, TA'd and tutored calculus, precalculus and college algebra, 2020–2026.</p></div></div>
      <div class="entry no-thumb"><div class="year">Duke</div><div><p>Tutored linear algebra and multivariable calculus, 2017–2020.</p></div></div>
      <div class="entry no-thumb quiet">
        <div class="year"></div>
        <details class="full">
          <summary>Full teaching history</summary>
          <ul>
            {rutgersTeaching.map((entry) => (
              <li>
                <b>{entry.term}</b> · {entry.href ? <a href={entry.href} target="_blank">{entry.role}</a> : entry.role}
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="timeline s-life" id="interests">
    <div class="side-label"><h2>Otherwise</h2><p>Off the clock</p></div>
    <div>
      <p class="life-text">
        Dodgeball, kickball, my local queer community, and getting outdoors as often as I can, most
        recently Sedona and Banff.
      </p>
      <div class="strip">
        <img src="/DH7A2568.jpg" alt="Playing dodgeball in a recreational league" loading="lazy" />
        <img src="/IMG_0070.jpg" alt="Hiking in Sedona, Arizona" loading="lazy" />
        <img src="/DH7A4652.jpg" alt="At a recreational kickball game" loading="lazy" />
        <img src="/IMG_0134.jpg" alt="At a lake in Banff, Canada" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

<script is:inline>
  (() => {
    // Replaces the static dependency-graph thumbnail with a live render of the GSpinGGP
    // blueprint's graph, so it tracks the formalization as it progresses. It fetches the
    // blueprint's DOT source, lays it out left-to-right with the blueprint's own scripts,
    // and frames the dense left part of the graph. The whole box links to the full graph.
    // If anything fails, the static PNG stays.
    const BASE = "https://sampease.github.io/GSpinGGP/blueprint/";
    const box = document.getElementById("gspinggp-graph");
    if (!box) return;

    const loadScript = (src) =>
      new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
        const s = document.createElement("script");
        s.src = src;
        s.onload = resolve;
        s.onerror = reject;
        document.head.appendChild(s);
      });

    async function render() {
      const html = await (await fetch(BASE + "dep_graph_document.html")).text();
      const start = html.indexOf("renderDot(`");
      const end = html.indexOf("`)", start);
      if (start < 0 || end < 0) throw new Error("graph source not found");
      const dot = html
        .slice(start + "renderDot(`".length, end)
        .replace("{", "{ graph [rankdir=LR];");

      for (const f of ["d3.min.js", "hpcc.min.js", "d3-graphviz.js"]) {
        await loadScript(BASE + "js/" + f);
      }

      const canvas = document.createElement("div");
      canvas.className = "dep-graph-canvas";
      box.appendChild(canvas);

      d3.select(canvas)
        .graphviz({ useWorker: false })
        .zoom(false)
        .width(canvas.clientWidth)
        .height(canvas.clientHeight)
        .renderDot(dot)
        .on("end", () => {
          const svg = canvas.querySelector("svg");
          if (!svg) return;
          // Frame the densest part of the graph (its left half), filling the box.
          // getBBox on the <svg> gives the drawn graph's extent in the SVG's own units.
          const bb = svg.getBBox();
          if (!bb.width) return;
          const w = bb.width * 0.53;
          const h = w * (canvas.clientHeight / canvas.clientWidth);
          svg.setAttribute("viewBox", `${bb.x + bb.width * 0.08} ${bb.y + bb.height * 0.08} ${w} ${h}`);
          svg.setAttribute("preserveAspectRatio", "xMidYMid slice");
          svg.setAttribute("width", "100%");
          svg.setAttribute("height", "100%");
          box.classList.add("is-live");
        });
    }

    const io = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
      if (entries.some((e) => e.isIntersecting)) {
        io.disconnect();
        render().catch((err) => console.warn("Live dependency graph unavailable:", err));
      }
    }, { rootMargin: "400px" });
    io.observe(box);
  })();
</script>

<style>
  .home {
    max-width: 920px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 20px;
  }

  a {
    color: var(--blue);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-color: rgba(60, 102, 168, 0.3);
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  a:hover {
    text-decoration-color: var(--blue);
  }

  /* Hero */
  .hero {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 230px;
    gap: 56px;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 44px 0 20px;
  }

  .hero h1 {
    font: 500 3.1rem/1.04 "Newsreader", serif;
    margin: 0 0 18px;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .hero h1 i {
    color: var(--blue);
  }

  .hero p {
    margin: 0 0 12px;
    font-size: 1.06rem;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .contact {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px 18px;
    margin-top: 18px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 14.5px;
  }

  .portrait {
    position: relative;
  }

  .portrait img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
    object-fit: cover;
    border-radius: 22px;
    display: block;
  }

  .portrait :global(.portrait-mark) {
    position: absolute;
    width: 70px;
    height: 70px;
    right: -18px;
    bottom: -18px;
    background: var(--paper);
    border-radius: 50%;
    padding: 10px;
  }

  /* Timeline sections */
  .timeline {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 150px 1fr;
    gap: 28px;
    padding: 44px 0 8px;
  }

  .timeline > * {
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .side-label {
    position: sticky;
    top: 20px;
    align-self: start;
  }

  .side-label h2 {
    font: italic 500 1.55rem/1.1 "Newsreader", serif;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .side-label p {
    margin: 4px 0 0;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .entries {
    border-left: 2px solid var(--line);
  }

  .entry {
    --dot: var(--sun);
    position: relative;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 64px 1fr 190px;
    gap: 16px;
    padding: 4px 0 22px 22px;
  }

  .entry.no-thumb {
    grid-template-columns: 64px 1fr;
  }

  .entry::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: -7px;
    top: 9px;
    width: 12px;
    height: 12px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--dot);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 4px var(--paper);
  }

  .s-math .entry { --dot: var(--blue); }
  .s-built .entry { --dot: var(--leaf); }
  .entry.quiet { --dot: var(--line); }

  .year {
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--muted);
    padding-top: 2px;
  }

  .entry h3 {
    font: 600 1.15rem/1.3 "Newsreader", serif;
    margin: 0 0 3px;
  }

  .entry h3 a {
    color: var(--ink);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-color: var(--sun);
    text-decoration-thickness: 2px;
    text-underline-offset: 4px;
  }

  .entry h3 a:hover {
    color: var(--blue);
    text-decoration-color: var(--blue);
  }

  .entry p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .entry p.more {
    margin-top: 8px;
  }

  .thumb-link {
    display: block;
    align-self: start;
  }

  .thumb {
    display: block;
    width: 190px;
    height: 127px;
    border-radius: 10px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    background: #fff;
    object-fit: contain;
    padding: 4px;
  }

  .thumb.fill {
    object-fit: cover;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .thumb-link:hover .thumb {
    border-color: var(--blue);
  }

  /* Live dependency graph in the dissertation thumbnail */
  .dep-graph {
    position: relative;
    width: 190px;
    height: 127px;
    border-radius: 10px;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    background: #fff;
  }

  .dep-graph .thumb {
    border: 0;
    border-radius: 0;
  }

  .dep-graph :global(.dep-graph-canvas) {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .dep-graph.is-live .thumb {
    visibility: hidden;
  }

  .dep-graph:hover {
    border-color: var(--blue);
  }

  details.full summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--blue);
  }

  details.full ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 10px 0 0;
  }

  details.full li {
    padding: 3px 0;
    font-size: 14.5px;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  details.full b {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .life-text {
    margin: 0 0 12px;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .strip {
    display: flex;
    gap: 10px;
    overflow-x: auto;
    padding: 4px 0 12px;
    scroll-snap-type: x mandatory;
  }

  .strip img {
    height: 200px;
    width: auto;
    border-radius: 12px;
    scroll-snap-align: start;
  }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .hero {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 26px;
      padding-top: 12px;
    }

    .portrait {
      order: -1;
      max-width: 170px;
    }

    .hero h1 {
      font-size: 2.4rem;
    }

    .timeline {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 14px;
    }

    .side-label {
      position: static;
    }

    .entry,
    .entry.no-thumb {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 4px;
    }

    .thumb,
    .dep-graph {
      width: 100%;
      height: 190px;
      margin-top: 8px;
    }

    .dep-graph .thumb {
      margin-top: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
